# The image copies one already-built binary in; nothing else in the repository
# belongs in the build context. Keeping it small matters more than usual here:
# `target/` alone is tens of gigabytes on a working checkout, and every byte of
# the context is sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
*

# The staged binary, which the `docker` release job puts here and the local
# build instructions in the Dockerfile copy here too.
!dist/
